[日本語版はこちら / Japanese version below](#日本語版-warikan-利用規約)

These Terms of Use ("Terms") are a legal agreement between you and Vladimir Rogozhkin, an independent developer ("we," "us"), governing your use of the WariKan mobile application ("the App"). By downloading, accessing, or using the App, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the App.

Our [Privacy Policy](https://jasik.github.io/warikan-policy/) explains how we handle your data and forms part of these Terms.

## 1. The Service

WariKan helps groups of travelers record shared expenses, split them, and track who owes whom. The App is provided free of charge at its core, with optional paid features described in Section 4.

**WariKan does not process, hold, or transfer money.** The App only records amounts and calculations; any actual reimbursement happens outside the App, directly between trip members, using whatever method they choose. We are not a payment service, money transmitter, or financial institution, and we are not a party to any settlement between users.

## 2. Accounts

You may sign in with Apple, sign in with Google, or continue as a **guest** (an anonymous account tied to your device). You are responsible for the activity that occurs under your account.

Guest accounts have an important limitation: because they are tied to your device and have no recoverable credentials, **deleting the App, resetting your device, or losing your device may permanently cut off access to a guest account and its server-side data**. To protect your data across devices, link your account to Apple or Google sign-in.

You may delete your account at any time in the App's settings. Deletion is handled as described in the Privacy Policy.

## 3. Your Content and Sharing

You retain ownership of the content you enter into the App (trip names, expenses, notes, payment reference details, etc.). You grant us the limited license needed to store, process, and display that content to operate the service — including showing it to the other members of trips you participate in, which is the App's core purpose.

You are responsible for the accuracy of what you enter, and for only inviting people you actually want to share trip data with. Expenses and settlements you record in a shared trip become part of the other members' trip history too, and may remain visible to them even if you later leave the trip or delete your account.

## 4. Purchases, Subscriptions, and Donations

The App offers optional paid items, processed by the Apple App Store or Google Play ("the Stores"):

- **Supporter donations** — one-time, consumable purchases that support development. Donations are voluntary, confer no additional obligation on us, and are **non-refundable** except where required by the Stores' policies or applicable law.
- **WariKan Pro** — an auto-renewable yearly subscription (currently ¥2,000/year; the exact price is always shown in the Store before purchase and may vary by region). Pro currently includes: unlimited active trips, exemption from automatic server-side archival of settled trip detail, and CSV export. We may adjust the exact set of Pro features over time; material reductions will be communicated in advance.

**Subscription mechanics (as required by the Stores):**

- Payment is charged to your Apple ID or Google account at confirmation of purchase.
- The subscription **renews automatically** unless auto-renew is turned off at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. Your account is charged for renewal within 24 hours prior to the end of the current period.
- You can manage or cancel the subscription in your App Store or Google Play account settings at any time; cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period. Deleting the App does not cancel a subscription.
- Refunds are handled by the Stores under their policies; we cannot issue refunds for purchases made through the Stores ourselves.

We do not receive or store your payment card details. Purchase entitlement status is processed via RevenueCat as described in the Privacy Policy.

## 5. Free-Tier Storage and Archival

To keep the free tier sustainable, detailed expense records of **settled (completed) trips** on free accounts may be automatically compressed/archived on our servers after a grace period (currently 30 days after completion). Summary information is retained, and full detail can be kept on your device via the App's "keep on device" option or restored by reopening the trip during the grace period. Pro accounts are exempt from this automatic archival. Details are described in the Privacy Policy.

## 6. Acceptable Use

You agree not to:

- use the App for any unlawful purpose, including money laundering or disguising the origin of funds;
